Terminal velocity v_T = \frac{2 r^2 (\rho_s - \rho_l) g}{9 \eta}.
Radius r = \frac{3.6\text{ mm}}{2} = 1.8 \times 10^{-3}\text{ m}.
\eta = \frac{2 (1.8 \times 10^{-3})^2 (7825 - 925) \times 9.8}{9 \times 2.45 \times 10^{-2}}
= \frac{2 \times 3.24 \times 10^{-6} \times 6900 \times 9.8}{0.2205}
= \frac{438.167 \times 10^{-3}}{0.2205} \approx 1.987 \approx 1.99\text{ Pa s}.

\frac{\Delta C}{C}_{\max} = \frac{\Delta p}{p} + 2\frac{\Delta q}{q} + 3\frac{\Delta r}{r} + \frac{1}{2}\frac{\Delta s}{s}
= 1\% + 2(2\%) + 3(3\%) + \frac{1}{2}(2\%)
= 1 + 4 + 9 + 1 = 15\%.

